# Milestone: v0.13.5-conformance-and-stdlib
# Covers: Integer shl/shr/ushr shift-count masking (Kotlin semantics).
#         ushr already masked to [0, 63]; shl/shr previously returned 0
#         for any count outside [0, 63) — now all three mask count &63.
#
# After the fix all three ops use: effective_count = raw_count & 63.
# Edge cases tested: count 63 (unchanged), count 64 (was 0 → identity
# shift), count 65 (was 0 → shift by 1), negative count (was 0 → mask
# wraps to [0, 63]).  Self value edge cases include positive and negative
# self with the boundary counts.
#
# ushr cases are included here to verify the Kotlin semantics hold at
# all three edge counts (these were already correct; they are coverage
# checks, not behavior changes).

# --- shl: count 63 (unchanged) ---
1.shl(63)
[00000000] -9223372036854775808

# --- shl: count 64 — was 0, now masks to 0 → identity shift ---
1.shl(64)
[00000001] 1

# --- shl: count 65 — was 0, now masks to 1 ---
1.shl(65)
[00000002] 2

# --- shl: negative count — was 0, now masks (-1 & 63 = 63) ---
1.shl(-1)
[00000003] -9223372036854775808

# --- shl: negative count, smaller wrap (-63 & 63 = 1) ---
1.shl(-63)
[00000004] 2

# --- shl: negative self with count 64 (identity) ---
(-8).shl(64)
[00000005] -8

# --- shr: count 63 (unchanged; logical right shift) ---
16.shr(63)
[00000006] 0

# --- shr: count 64 — was 0, now masks to 0 → identity shift ---
1.shr(64)
[00000007] 1

# --- shr: count 64 on non-trivial value ---
16.shr(64)
[00000008] 16

# --- shr: negative self with count 64 ---
(-8).shr(64)
[00000009] -8

# --- ushr: count 64 — already Kotlin-masked (64 & 63 = 0 → identity) ---
(-1).ushr(64)
[00000010] -1

# --- ushr: count 65 — already masked (65 & 63 = 1) ---
(-1).ushr(65)
[00000011] 9223372036854775807

# --- ushr: negative count — already masked ((-1) & 63 = 63) ---
(-1).ushr(-1)
[00000012] 1
